Here's a code snippet that shows how to create a simple interface displaying the "UP" and "DOWN" buttons with a text area in between using Qt in C++:

```
#include <QApplication>
#include <QWidget>
#include <QPushButton>
#include <QTextEdit>
#include <QVBoxLayout>

int main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
    QApplication app(argc, argv);

    QWidget window;
    window.setWindowTitle("Up Down Buttons");

    // Create buttons
    QPushButton *upButton = new QPushButton("UP");
    QPushButton *downButton = new QPushButton("DOWN");

    // Create text area
    QTextEdit *textArea = new QTextEdit();

    // Add buttons and text area to a vertical layout
    QVBoxLayout *layout = new QVBoxLayout();
    layout->addWidget(upButton);
    layout->addWidget(textArea);
    layout->addWidget(downButton);

    // Set widget layout
    window.setLayout(layout);

    window.show();

    return app.exec();
}
```

This code creates a `QPushButton` for the "UP" button and another one for the "DOWN" button, as well as a `QTextEdit` for the text area. It then adds these widgets to a vertical layout using `QVBoxLayout`, and sets this layout as the widget's layout using `setLayout()`. Finally, it shows the widget and starts the Qt event loop using `show()` and `app.exec()` respectively.

Here is a C program that takes an array as input and calculates the sum of all of its elements:

```
#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    int array[] = {2, 4, 3, 7, 5};
    int i, sum = 0;
    int n = sizeof(array)/sizeof(array[0]);

    for (i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        sum += array[i];
    }

    printf("Sum of all array elements = %d\n", sum);
    return 0;
}
```
In the above program, we first declare an array with 5 elements `{2,4,3,7,5}`. We also declare two integer variables `i` and `sum`. The variable `i` is used as a counter in the `for` loop and `sum` is used to store the final result of the sum of all array elements. To calculate the number of elements in the array, we divide the size of the entire array by the size of one element using the `sizeof()` function. The `for loop` is used to iterate over each element of the array and add its value to the `sum` variable. Finally, we print the value of `sum` which gives us the sum of all elements in the array.

